hysical permission-ID reconciliation carried forward as a controlled catalogue item.** || RUMAHAGEN_WF03_M10_FULL_REBUILD_CONTROLLED_v1.1/SOURCE_M10_ONLY/RUMAHAGEN_WF-03.2_M10D_FINAL_CROSS_RECONCILIATION_v1.0.md:230: Emergency broken dependency is a recovery condition and is not automatically interpreted as a normal no-preset state. || RUMAHAGEN_WF03_M10_FULL_REBUILD_CONTROLLED_v1.1/RUMAHAGEN_WF03_M10_FULL_REBUILD_CONTROLLED_v1.1.md:303: > M10 is the canonical authorization boundary. Role is actor grouping; Role Permission is the default permission matrix/baseline; Permission Preset is an optional configurable custom authorization configuration targeted to an existing role. A preset never creates a new role and only configures the permissions established for that role. Superadmin has Full Governance. Manager may Create, Edit, Delete and Assign Permission Presets for Agent only. Admin, Buyer, Developer Partner, Instructor and Agent do not manage presets. Permission Preset has mandatory UI/UX configuration, starts from the role default matrix, supports governed permission/scope configuration and effective-permission preview, and is enforced by API/server-side authorization and RLS. Authorization resolves from the authenticated account's role, optional preset and governed domain conditions. Preset lifecycle is separate from account lifecycle; used presets have no normal delete; emergency recovery must fail closed when required and must never grant automatic extra authority. Physical and runtime proof remain downstream and are not semantic blockers. M10 v1.1 is COMPLETE / LOCKED.",,RETAIN_CORE_ONLY,YES,N/A,YES,NO,NO,PRESERVE_NO_DELTA_REQUIRED
